% Changelog (reverse chronological):
% 2026-08-23 - Claude: created, at Jan's request, as a companion BibTeX database for the arXiv
%   submission folder -- exactly the 11 references actually \bibitem-ed in
%   article/lattice_line_covers_extended.tex, converted from that inline thebibliography (kept
%   verbatim there; NOT wired into this .bib via \bibliography{}/\bibliographystyle{}). Deliberate:
%   arXiv does not run BibTeX itself, so a submission that depends on one either has to include a
%   pre-built .bbl (a known source of drift/failure if it goes stale relative to the .bib) or risks
%   an uncompilable upload; the inline thebibliography sidesteps that class of problem entirely,
%   and this file exists for reference/reuse (e.g. importing into a reference manager) rather than
%   to drive the compile. Six of the eleven entries already existed, near-identically, in
%   ../../../ai-workspace/projects/lattice-line-covers/literature/references.bib (that file covers
%   the full research corpus, not just what's cited here) -- reused verbatim where they matched;
%   Eisenbud1995, Robbiano1985, gitrepo, report2026, zenodo added fresh from the manuscript's own
%   \bibitem text, since none of the five existed in that file yet.

